{"id": "EUVD-2026-27787", "enisaUuid": "d19b86a9-a5ff-3efc-85e0-1c49c55cd32c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhfs: Replace BUG_ON with error handling for CNID count checks\n\nIn a06ec283e125 next_id, folder_count, and file_count in the super block\ninfo were expanded to 64 bits, and BUG_ONs were added to detect\noverflow. This triggered an error reported by syzbot: if the MDB is\ncorrupted, the BUG_ON is triggered. This patch replaces this mechanism\nwith proper error handling and resolves the syzbot reported bug.\n\nSinged-off-by: Jori Koolstra <jkoolstra@xs4all.nl>", "datePublished": "2026-05-06T11:28:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T10:07:13", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/559f856b109c45844816a1693e259f93d3556c61", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6536c1ced315fa645576d3a39c6e07f2a472962", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b226804532a875c10276168dc55ce752944096bd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-43228", "GHSA-g4p6-4x9w-qfq5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "182a6e47-d636-3baa-ab31-57ec7f9edb80", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "495aab49-cbdd-35e9-a5c4-c0e979b21222", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.6"}, {"id": "6e953605-7668-3594-a2f7-6509373125db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a06ec283e125e334155fe13005c76c9f484ce759 <559f856b109c45844816a1693e259f93d3556c61"}, {"id": "743df626-0cc4-3aa1-81d6-8b5358c4fbe1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a06ec283e125e334155fe13005c76c9f484ce759 <b6536c1ced315fa645576d3a39c6e07f2a472962"}, {"id": "8196e19f-caa9-34f3-bdac-fd3a85acc3a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "aaed2055-2f63-3a06-83c3-39b68d18a0be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "ve